people on both sides of the political  divide feeling tense  anxious and overwhelmed right now but  how do you know when that stress is  becoming a serious mental health issue  in today's health watch denise valdez  shares some startling statistics  well brian a global pandemic is  stressful enough but then you add a  presidential election to the mix  an election that's really divided  families and communities and you can  feel like you're in a real pressure  cooker  so the term election stress disorder is  becoming widely used  widely accepted in fact a recent study  shows just how stressed americans are  feeling  so the american psychological  association conducted the  stress in america study and it shows  that nearly 70 percent of all adults  surveyed  feel the election is a significant  source of stress right now in fact  it found that 76 percent of democrats  and 67 percent of republicans  along with 64 percent of independents  believe this election is a significant  stressor  now stephanie waite is a licensed  therapist in sherman texas  it's a lot to process i think people are  getting it from  not just the media and from television  but from their neighbors and from their  friends and people at the stores it's  just  you almost can't get away everywhere you  that's it and  it's everywhere we turn wherever we go  there's something that's a big deal and  and i'm hearing a lot too we can't you  don't have a lot of control  over these things we don't know the  outcome or when things are going to  be different or what that's going to  look like and so i think that  uncertainty  makes it hard because you don't know how  to plan  you don't know how you know what to  expect and novelty just feels really  uncomfortable  so election stress can translate to  trouble sleeping people being cranky or  irritable  also feeling anxious about being around  folks who might not share your same  political view  so some ways to cope will dr waite  suggest focus on the things that you can  control  you might need to just to give social  media a break maybe even place some  boundaries on what you're going to be  talking about with certain people  be sure to exercise maybe even try some  meditation and if you feel you're really  at a breaking point  talk to someone like a counselor to get  you back in balance
 

